# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://aka.ms/winget-manifest.defaultLocale.1.10.0.schema.json
#
# Tandem Commander - winget default-locale manifest template.
# Generated into tools/winget/manifests/<version>/ by tools/winget/publish.ps1,
# which strips every comment except the schema line above - so authoring notes
# stay here and never reach the submitted manifest. Consequence: no line inside
# a block scalar may start with '#'.
# Placeholders: VERSION, RELEASE_SUMMARY
#
# This file is the source of truth for every piece of catalogue metadata.
# RELEASE_SUMMARY is the lead paragraph of this version's CHANGELOG.md section,
# flattened to one paragraph and indented by two spaces by the generator.
# Publisher must stay "Pavel Stupka": winget-pkgs validation compares it with
# the installer's AppPublisher and with the code-signing certificate subject.
#
# PrivacyUrl points at PRIVACY.md on main (feature 083). The catalogue's
# moderators ask packages that store credentials - FTP/SFTP passwords here -
# for a privacy disclosure (specs/072-winget-distribution/REMAINING-WORK.md
# section P0 item 3). The URL is literal, not versioned: the statement always
# describes the current release. PRIVACY.md is a public claim and must be
# updated in the same change as anything its update rule lists (CLAUDE.md,
# "Privacy statement"). The URL answers 200 only once PRIVACY.md is on main.
#
# NO THIRD-PARTY BRAND OR PRODUCT NAMES in ShortDescription, Description or
# Tags. The first submission named the program's ancestry (Norton Commander,
# Open Salamander, Altap Salamander), archiver products (7-Zip, RAR) and the
# command shell presets (Command Prompt, PowerShell, Windows Terminal, Git
# Bash), and carried the tags explorer-replacement, open-salamander and
# salamander. The moderator asked for the Description to be rewritten without
# them (winget-pkgs#426090, 2026-10-06: "the Policy 1.2 check might be due to
# the several brands mentioned in the Description"). Describe what the program
# does; generic format and protocol names (FTP, SFTP, Markdown, Unicode) and
# the platform (Windows) are fine. The origin stays where it belongs: the
# Copyright line (required attribution) and the repository's licence files.

PackageIdentifier: PavelStupka.TandemCommander
PackageVersion: {{VERSION}}
PackageLocale: en-US
Publisher: Pavel Stupka
PublisherUrl: https://tandemcommander.org/
PublisherSupportUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/issues
PrivacyUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/blob/main/PRIVACY.md
Author: Pavel Stupka
PackageName: Tandem Commander
PackageUrl: https://tandemcommander.org/
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
LicenseUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/blob/main/LICENSE
Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 Pavel Stupka; portions (c) Open Salamander Authors
CopyrightUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/blob/main/LICENSE
ShortDescription: Fast, keyboard-driven two-panel file manager for Windows with archive browsing, file viewers and plugins.
Description: |-
  Tandem Commander is an open-source two-panel (dual-pane) file manager for
  Windows. It is a native application - there is no runtime to install and it
  starts instantly.

  Both panels show a directory, and every operation - copy, move, delete,
  rename, pack, unpack, compare - works between them and can be driven entirely
  from the keyboard. Common archive formats are browsed like ordinary folders.
  A plugin architecture adds file viewers, FTP and SFTP clients, checksum
  tools, a Markdown viewer and more.

  It offers full Unicode and long-path support, a dark theme, sync-status
  badges for cloud-synced folders, and a configurable command shell.

  Tandem Commander is built with AI-assisted, spec-driven development under
  human direction and review, and is provided "as is", without warranty of any
  kind.
Moniker: tandemcommander
Tags:
  - archiver
  - commander
  - dual-pane
  - file-manager
  - file-viewer
  - filemanager
  - ftp
  - keyboard
  - orthodox-file-manager
  - sftp
  - two-panel
  - windows
  - zip
ReleaseNotes: |-
{{RELEASE_SUMMARY}}
ReleaseNotesUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}}
Documentations:
  - DocumentLabel: Changelog
    DocumentUrl: https://github.com/tandemcommander/tandemcommander/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
InstallationNotes: |-
  The Markdown viewer renders through the Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime,
  which is part of Windows 11. On Windows 10 install it once with:
  winget install Microsoft.EdgeWebView2Runtime
ManifestType: defaultLocale
ManifestVersion: 1.10.0
